{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/921709-2-ed-possession","id":921709,"title":"[2 ed.] Possession","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-26T15:07:55-07:00","id":921709,"title":"[2 ed.] Possession","content":"Hi all,<br /> if I'm not wrong in the first edition, possession doesn't apply against other vampires. In second edition it isn't written anything that let you understand this. It simply says that the roll is Intelligence + Intimidation + Dominate \u2013 victim\u2019s Resolve. And in the text it says that: &quot;If she attempts to kill herself the victim may roll Resolve + Blood Potency as a reflexive action, on a success he evicts the vampire from his consciousness&quot; so it means that is definetly possible to possess another vampire body. The question is: isn't too eays for an average vampire to possess the body of an ancient vampire. I means., with an average dice pool of 10-12 dice, subtracting 5 for resolve it's quite easy to obtain a success with 5-7 dice. <br /> Am I missing something?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T15:12:13-07:00","id":921713,"title":"","content":"First you have to actually get Dominate 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T15:16:17-07:00","id":921714,"title":"","content":"In a white room setting it would arguably be quite easy to possess even a much older kindred.<br /> I think the difficulty comes from the fact that most powerful kindred will seldomly be unguarded or otherwise vulnerable to being body snatched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T15:24:04-07:00","id":921717,"title":"","content":"The elder needs to be Mesmerized first, which gets contested with BP, so that's the first line of defense. Mesmerizing isn't enough by itself to prevent the subject from inflicting damage on himself enough to snap out of it either. But yeah, if you can get in there, you're probably golden. You can still only use their mundane abilities, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T15:37:11-07:00","id":921719,"title":"","content":"Oh right. I missed the mesmerize prerequisite. Sorry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T17:18:41-07:00","id":921763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/921709-2-ed-possession?p=921717#post921717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mesmerizing isn't enough by itself to prevent the subject from inflicting damage on himself enough to snap out of it either.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting point, but I would dispute it. While mesmerized doesn't turn the victim into a vegetable, but just renders them susceptible to simple orders, I would tend to think that the victim isn't aware it's being controled, even if they were expecting it. I mean, otherwise, since it takes a turn to issue a command after succeeding the mesmerized roll (bar exceptionnal success), any somewhat savvy victim would just slap themselves immediately and gain the bonus for further dominate attempts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T17:55:40-07:00","id":921778,"title":"","content":"Right, but if there's one thing an elder will be wary of, it's Dominate. A mortal or or even a neonate might not expect it, or even be aware of it's existence, and would be complacent. An elder should not be, having been witness and likely subject to it more than once in their Requiem. Perhaps a Wits + Composure to detect, or Resolve + Composure to attempt self-harm could cover the grey area.<br /> <br /> I would prefer that vampires had the opportunity to break Dominate like they can Majesty. It's limited, and it's BP scaled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T18:25:33-07:00","id":921792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/921709-2-ed-possession?p=921717#post921717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The elder needs to be Mesmerized first, which gets contested with BP, so that's the first line of defense. Mesmerizing isn't enough by itself to prevent the subject from inflicting damage on himself enough to snap out of it either. But yeah, if you can get in there, you're probably golden. You can still only use their mundane abilities, however.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a whole thread about this and how you act while mesmerized. They are not aware of being controlled. They cant even remember what happened while controlled. I think it would take an exceptional roll on Occult or something to know what is happening to you. I agree with Verge that There should be rolls to try to hurt yourself even if you did know what happened.<br /> <br /> It's hard to mesmerize an Elder and getting to Dominate 5 isnt easy. so really it's not that easy to possess a vampire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T20:36:18-07:00","id":921832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/921709-2-ed-possession?p=921763#post921763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting point, but I would dispute it. While mesmerized doesn't turn the victim into a vegetable, but just renders them susceptible to simple orders, I would tend to think that the victim isn't aware it's being controled, even if they were expecting it. I mean, otherwise, since it takes a turn to issue a command after succeeding the mesmerized roll (bar exceptionnal success), any somewhat savvy victim would just slap themselves immediately and gain the bonus for further dominate attempts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who needs to issue a command? Just Mesmerise and immediately use Possession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T15:11:58-07:00","id":922241,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's no way I'd allow both to be used in the same turn as a GM. Mesmerize needs an extra turn to issue a command, so I rule that the same goes when you use the other levels on top of it. Except maybe if mesmerize nets an exceptionnal success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T20:10:27-07:00","id":922393,"title":"","content":"Possession is a reflexive action. Unless I am hugely mistaken.. You can take an instant and reflexive in one turn.<br /> <br /> Awe and Idol for example can be done in one turn too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 06-27-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T20:29:34-07:00","id":922408,"title":"","content":"You can certainly do both in the same turn, you can even Mesmerise them on your turn then wait and Possess them on their own turn. Possessing someone is as easy as spending a bit of vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T06:54:35-07:00","id":923822,"title":"","content":"I find the &quot;Getting to Dominate 5 is hard&quot; argument pretty strange. The book does not speak of any difficulties or problems to obtain high level disciplines, so on some tables it's as hard as getting 6 XP (if you started out with a Discipline at three). Assuming it's hard to get in a more or less baseline game discussion doesn't help much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T08:12:00-07:00","id":923859,"title":"","content":"Yes. It's not something every vampire has but there's not much in the way of roadblocks once you've gained access to Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T09:16:06-07:00","id":923896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/921709-2-ed-possession?p=923822#post923822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the &amp;quot;Getting to Dominate 5 is hard&amp;quot; argument pretty strange. The book does not speak of any difficulties or problems to obtain high level disciplines, so on some tables it's as hard as getting 6 XP (if you started out with a Discipline at three). Assuming it's hard to get in a more or less baseline game discussion doesn't help much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm the only one who made that argument, and I think you may have misunderstood what I was getting at. It's not that Dominate 5 is inherently hard to get (thank goodness 2e got rid of exponentially increasing XP costs), it's that it's far from universally accessible. You have to either play a Ventrue or drink one's Vitae, and then it costs 6-15 experiences for a Ventrue or 16-20 for another vampire, which could be going towards getting you other 5th dot powers (which are also quite effective against elders) or increasing Blood Potency to narrow the gap between yourself and elders. Plus, experience purchases need to be justified in the narrative, and while different groups will have different standards for justifying 5th dot Discipline purchases, any way you slice it, Dominate 5 represents a significant commitment of meta-game resources and narrative investment. In my opinion, players who dedicate that much time and energy into being good at mind controlling people should be <i>very</i> good at mind controlling people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:49:01-07:00","id":923995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/921709-2-ed-possession?p=923896#post923896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'm the only one who made that argument, and I think you may have misunderstood what I was getting at. It's not that Dominate 5 is inherently hard to get (thank goodness 2e got rid of exponentially increasing XP costs), it's that it's far from universally accessible. You have to either play a Ventrue or drink one's Vitae, and then it costs 6-15 experiences for a Ventrue or 16-20 for another vampire, which could be going towards getting you other 5th dot powers (which are also quite effective against elders) or increasing Blood Potency to narrow the gap between yourself and elders. Plus, experience purchases need to be justified in the narrative, and while different groups will have different standards for justifying 5th dot Discipline purchases, any way you slice it, Dominate 5 represents a significant commitment of meta-game resources and narrative investment. In my opinion, players who dedicate that much time and energy into being good at mind controlling people should be <i>very</i> good at mind controlling people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also said that &quot;it wasn't easy&quot; I didn't mean hard, exactly, but I meant more what you explained there. A lot of time and effort invested in getting there both in game and out of game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T18:10:40-07:00","id":925142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/921709-2-ed-possession?p=923896#post923896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'm the only one who made that argument, and I think you may have misunderstood what I was getting at. It's not that Dominate 5 is inherently hard to get (thank goodness 2e got rid of exponentially increasing XP costs), it's that it's far from universally accessible. You have to either play a Ventrue or drink one's Vitae, and then it costs 6-15 experiences for a Ventrue or 16-20 for another vampire, which could be going towards getting you other 5th dot powers (which are also quite effective against elders) or increasing Blood Potency to narrow the gap between yourself and elders. Plus, experience purchases need to be justified in the narrative, and while different groups will have different standards for justifying 5th dot Discipline purchases, any way you slice it, Dominate 5 represents a significant commitment of meta-game resources and narrative investment. In my opinion, players who dedicate that much time and energy into being good at mind controlling people should be <i>very</i> good at mind controlling people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry for the possible threat derailment (maybe this should warrant its own thread?:<br /> <br /> Could you (or anyone else in here) present some good examples of how to represnt the acquisition of high level disciplines in-game? So far, whenever one of my group members managed to gain access to such powerful 'high-end' abilities, it always felt a bit flat to me. At the same time, I was hesitant as the storyteller to restrict their character progression too much because I couldn't provide any guidance on how to turn the experience into a better narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T08:47:46-07:00","id":925362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lepaca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/921709-2-ed-possession?p=925142#post925142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry for the possible threat derailment (maybe this should warrant its own thread?:<br /> <br /> Could you (or anyone else in here) present some good examples of how to represnt the acquisition of high level disciplines in-game? So far, whenever one of my group members managed to gain access to such powerful 'high-end' abilities, it always felt a bit flat to me. At the same time, I was hesitant as the storyteller to restrict their character progression too much because I couldn't provide any guidance on how to turn the experience into a better narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the most current game that I am playing in, my character is a Daeva and I have been building up Majesty. From the beginning, my personal goal was to get Idol so I started with 3 in majesty. Every fight we had I would charm my way out of it or try to talk my way out of it. I used it A LOT. I actually didnt use dot 3 very much, my next purchase was BP 2 so i could Majesty 4 in one turn. Then I took majesty 4 and continued to use it to get myself out of fights or stop fights by making everyone my best friend or having their friends save me. I purchased Idol and eventually got into a situation with more people than I could charm my way out of and had my character just... sort of pop Idol out of desperation. It seemed fitting in the narrative. I hope this helps some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T13:11:09-07:00","id":925476,"title":"","content":"My suggestion for you would be to try and visualize how you would teach a power if you knew it. That's the method I used and was emulated by others in my group. Occasionally one could spike and develop a power out of sequence but you couldn't ever rely on it until you purchased it and any of the attendant ranks.<br /> <br /> One of my characters wanted to learn Protean (first edition version) after witnessing a kindred transform into a veritable nest of fleas and escape. After some horse trading, her sire managed to get a Gangrel Dragon teacher with a reputation for &quot;unorthodox&quot; teaching methods, agree to teach her Protean to mastery level. (Which is in character terminology for 5 ranks in a discipline.) At their first meeting, my character learned to channel her Beast's reaction as bluffing aggression to hide fear and repress the flight response. (Easy enough since they had never met before and the power had been paid for in xp.) In their first formal lesson she had my character dig a hole 6 ft. deep, then about an hour before sunrise, she shoved my character in the hole and told her to find a way out before sunrise by merging with the dirt or be stuck outside during the day under loosely packed dirt then proceeded to bury my character. My character temporarily manifested the protean claws that evening trying to dig herself out but didn't meld in the soil. Another session, she encased my character in a box with quick drying cement. Then threw the box into the lake. She triggered the animal transformation by setting a pack of hunting dogs on her and informing my character she had to escape them using no powers except protean before they tree'd her and melding into something counted as being tree'd.<br /> Mist form just had her locked in a steam room that kept increasing in temperature and she had to escape through grated vents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-03-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:27:51-07:00","id":925664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lepaca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/921709-2-ed-possession?p=925142#post925142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you (or anyone else in here) present some good examples of how to represnt the acquisition of high level disciplines in-game? So far, whenever one of my group members managed to gain access to such powerful 'high-end' abilities, it always felt a bit flat to me. At the same time, I was hesitant as the storyteller to restrict their character progression too much because I couldn't provide any guidance on how to turn the experience into a better narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div> I take the name Discipline very literally here. Disciplines are learned through practice and, well, discipline. While the books talk about the power of the Beast and the like, I simply describe Disciplines as a vampire exercising their psychic abilities through force of will. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:40:52-07:00","id":925669,"title":"","content":"There's a nice section in The Blood about the psychology of Disciplines, how each affects and changes the vampire that learns them. There's a few ideas scattered across the books explaining how a vampire doesn't just learn a Discipline the way a human learns gardening, specifically, 'The Damned don\u2019t learn Animalism the way a human learns typing, or gardening; he doesn\u2019t attend classes and practice, practice, practice. He literally awakens a part of his monstrous heritage that lies slumbering in his Blood. He stirs a part of himself that was once hidden, a part that finds sympathy forged between the Beast within and all those little Beasts without.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T17:03:00-07:00","id":926170,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies, very insightful!<br /> <br /> So basically seems like there are two takes on this:<br /> <br /> 1) Training, tutoring and discipline. Unlocking a new discipline is basically an analogue to learning a new skill or fighting style. I can see how this could be incorporated into a chronicle or even as a story hook. If taken to an extreme, the risk of this approach could be that the chronicle could devolve into a kind of 80s training montage with characters focused solely on self improvement.<br /> <br /> 2) Almost the complete opposite. Disciplines are inherent ability sets that come with having a Beast within and by unlocking that potential. (Granted the quote pertained to Animalism specifically but I can see it being applied to all Kindred abilities). I would assume that in actual this gameplay this would result in characters almost reflexively unlocking new powers without much active control from their side (albeit interest would likely help), would you agree, nofather?<br /> <br /> So as with many things in CoD it seems to come down to player group choice (which I love!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T17:35:33-07:00","id":926179,"title":"","content":"The two stances aren't quite opposites. <br /> <br /> You do need to have an inherant ability. Thankfully, though, all Disciplines are growths of inherant vampire abilities: Majesty, Nightmare, Dominate and Obfuscate are all variations of controlling one's Predator's Aura (Dominating, Beastly, Seductive, and negating). The four physicals relate to a healing and blood buffing to push your body further. Auspex reflects hightened vampire senses taken to an extreme, and Animalism reflects the corruptive nature of the Curse to spread. The five signature Disciplines do need a small boost as well to learn them in the form of taking a bit of vitae from someone that knows it. <br /> <br /> However, like just about any other talent you might have, you need to train it. Natural ability only goes so far without practice and training. Sure, you have to practice with mastering your Beast and Lashing Out and similar, but that's still just practice using a mystical force rather than mundane talent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T17:56:36-07:00","id":926183,"title":"","content":"A simple way to avoid entire sessions devolving into a bad remake of Rocky is to not run the training sessions during game time for the main storyline. They can be done as solo sessions or side quests. Or simply narrate something to that effect occurs in down time. One of the advantages of using NPC teachers is that the ST can set their availability and decide when they have other obligations to address instead of teaching. (So players get back to the main story.) If they're training in a given discipline but haven't yet paid for it, you're free to situationally allow or disallow the player to use the power in question according to the needs of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:34:09-07:00","id":929812,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear: Possession does apply against Kindred. Lots of good commentary in this thread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}